(7467708, 1184682, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An excellent image that contributes well to the open challenge<br/> <br/>Wow! That must have been some moment when he surfaced so close to you, I don''t know how much time you had but well done for getting such a good shot quickly. Your technical settings are just right with adequate DOF, low ISO and fast enough shutter speed and your focus is spot on, all in all a great shot. The reflections are gorgeous and the greens of the water are superb. I know this is the open challenge and there must be some good stuff for this to end up at 19 but you do have a respectable score, well done Ronnie.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An excellent image that contributes well to the open challenge Wow! That must have been some moment when he surfaced so close to you, I don''t know how much time you had but well done for getting such a good shot quickly. Your technical settings are just right with adequate DOF, low ISO and fast enough shutter speed and your focus is spot on, all in all a great shot. The reflections are gorgeous and the greens of the water are superb. I know this is the open challenge and there must be some good stuff for this to end up at 19 but you do have a respectable score, well done Ronnie.', '2016-08-08 06:34:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(7467710, 1184799, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An excellent image that contributes well to the open challenge<br/> <br/>Welcome to DPC! And what a good start with your virgin entry, its nicely composed and captures the essence of the moment well. Your DOF is good giving sufficient clarity for where he''s headed with just a little softness in the background or should I say his foreground which isolates him well, the reflections are good with nice ripples. The ''decisive moment'' has also been well timed at the end of his paddle stroke. The only concern I do have is with those ripples the highlights are blown, perhaps a stop of minus exposure compensation would have helped to preserve some detail here.<br/> <br/>Thank you Tammie for your great contribution to the challenge and DPC and I look forward to seeing more from you soon.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An excellent image that contributes well to the open challenge Welcome to DPC! And what a good start with your virgin entry, its nicely composed and captures the essence of the moment well. Your DOF is good giving sufficient clarity for where he''s headed with just a little softness in the background or should I say his foreground which isolates him well, the reflections are good with nice ripples. The ''decisive moment'' has also been well timed at the end of his paddle stroke. The only concern I do have is with those ripples the highlights are blown, perhaps a stop of minus exposure compensation would have helped to preserve some detail here. Thank you Tammie for your great contribution to the challenge and DPC and I look forward to seeing more from you soon.', '2016-08-08 06:57:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(7467712, 1185190, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that contributes well to the open challenge<br/> <br/>You''ve managed to capture good detail throughout your image through the use of HDR to avoid the limitations of the camera''s dynamic range. The composition is good with the obelisk off-centre and room for the lovely wide open landscape surrounding it. The grass has taken on a scarlet swathe that  reflects the sun''s rays but feels somewhat overdone, I think it would benefit from a little easing back on the saturation. Also, the sharpening has left halos throughout the horizon most noticeable towards the edges. Thanks for your entry Eugene</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that contributes well to the open challenge You''ve managed to capture good detail throughout your image through the use of HDR to avoid the limitations of the camera''s dynamic range. The composition is good with the obelisk off-centre and room for the lovely wide open landscape surrounding it. The grass has taken on a scarlet swathe that  reflects the sun''s rays but feels somewhat overdone, I think it would benefit from a little easing back on the saturation. Also, the sharpening has left halos throughout the horizon most noticeable towards the edges. Thanks for your entry Eugene', '2016-08-08 07:06:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(7467713, 1184816, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An excellent image that contributes well to the open challenge<br/> <br/>What a great idea and what great execution, this is a wonderful image well deserved of its high score and high placing. It''s excellent that you''ve got them all looking in the same direction at the same time, all eagerly seeking something though what we know not but the true excellence that really makes the image superb is the bloke in the basement smiling direct at the camera, he''s fooled the lot of ''em! Wonderful! I love the derelict nature of the house itself but rather wish I could see a little more of the superb backdrop of its location. The only thing I can think of to improve this is the title itself you could have helped the viewer with some reference to what they''re all looking for, for example, the fisherman''s return or something that refers to his guile in deceiving them all. <br/> <br/>Anyway, an excellent entry Benedikt, thank you for amusing and delighting us all here,</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An excellent image that contributes well to the open challenge What a great idea and what great execution, this is a wonderful image well deserved of its high score and high placing. It''s excellent that you''ve got them all looking in the same direction at the same time, all eagerly seeking something though what we know not but the true excellence that really makes the image superb is the bloke in the basement smiling direct at the camera, he''s fooled the lot of ''em! Wonderful! I love the derelict nature of the house itself but rather wish I could see a little more of the superb backdrop of its location. The only thing I can think of to improve this is the title itself you could have helped the viewer with some reference to what they''re all looking for, for example, the fisherman''s return or something that refers to his guile in deceiving them all.  Anyway, an excellent entry Benedikt, thank you for amusing and delighting us all here,', '2016-08-08 07:17:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(7467714, 1185046, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that contributes well to the open challenge<br/> <br/>Yet another lovely landscape from this wonderful part of the world. An appealing composition featuring the pool in the top of the, presumably extinct, volcano together with the laval rocks evokes a sense of other worldliness. The rich ruby red skies with their softened reflections adds to the overall effect. Thanks for your entry Otto</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that contributes well to the open challenge Yet another lovely landscape from this wonderful part of the world. An appealing composition featuring the pool in the top of the, presumably extinct, volcano together with the laval rocks evokes a sense of other worldliness. The rich ruby red skies with their softened reflections adds to the overall effect. Thanks for your entry Otto', '2016-08-08 07:22:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(7467715, 1184738, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that contributes well to the open challenge<br/> <br/>A good frontal bird study that captures his profile well though his eye just seems a tad on the soft side, the feathers under his beak appear sharper than those in the vicinity of his eye just a slight bringing forward of the focus would have sharpened the eye just enough to give it that bit more impact. I feel the exposure is also ever so slightly a little on the bright side just easing back a fraction would have improved it to add to the impact. Overall, a great image Tony so very near, thanks for your entry</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that contributes well to the open challenge A good frontal bird study that captures his profile well though his eye just seems a tad on the soft side, the feathers under his beak appear sharper than those in the vicinity of his eye just a slight bringing forward of the focus would have sharpened the eye just enough to give it that bit more impact. I feel the exposure is also ever so slightly a little on the bright side just easing back a fraction would have improved it to add to the impact. Overall, a great image Tony so very near, thanks for your entry', '2016-08-08 07:29:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(7467718, 1184801, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that contributes well to the open challenge<br/> <br/>It''s that church again! Very different from the previous composition but again emphasising the proximity of its overwhelming neighbours. I quite like your composition it works to a degree but I''m imagining myself in the same situation and I can see potential there to emphasise the overwhelming size of the big building to the left. Using the church''s reflection either together with the church or even completely excluding the church itself concentrating on the reflection and building alone, I don''t know if you could get yourself in a position to be able to achieve that? It may well be that you are restricted in the position you can get to but their does seem some untapped potential there still. Thanks for your entry Marcel</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that contributes well to the open challenge It''s that church again! Very different from the previous composition but again emphasising the proximity of its overwhelming neighbours. I quite like your composition it works to a degree but I''m imagining myself in the same situation and I can see potential there to emphasise the overwhelming size of the big building to the left. Using the church''s reflection either together with the church or even completely excluding the church itself concentrating on the reflection and building alone, I don''t know if you could get yourself in a position to be able to achieve that? It may well be that you are restricted in the position you can get to but their does seem some untapped potential there still. Thanks for your entry Marcel', '2016-08-08 07:38:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(7467719, 1184415, 156466, '<td valign="top">As I watched my score and kept my fingers crossed that this might be the month I actually win a Free Study, this is the image that had me worried.  Congratulations on a well deserved Blue.  Wonderful shot.</td>', 'As I watched my score and kept my fingers crossed that this might be the month I actually win a Free Study, this is the image that had me worried.  Congratulations on a well deserved Blue.  Wonderful shot.', '2016-08-08 07:39:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(7467720, 1184729, 156466, '<td valign="top">As I watched my score and kept my fingers crossed that this might be the month I actually win a Free Study, this is the other image that had me worried.  Congratulations on the Yellow.  Wonderful shot, and my pick for Blue. Absolute perfect processing.</td>', 'As I watched my score and kept my fingers crossed that this might be the month I actually win a Free Study, this is the other image that had me worried.  Congratulations on the Yellow.  Wonderful shot, and my pick for Blue. Absolute perfect processing.', '2016-08-08 07:42:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(7467721, 1185155, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that contributes well to the open challenge<br/> <br/>A great sky that you''ve done well to bring out the lovely detail without blowing the highlights. The sliver of foreground serves well as an interesting base that has plenty to keep our interest until we inevitably look up to that fascinating sky whose textures and variety of colours are really quite captivating. A great exposure and composition well done and thanks for your entry Janine</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that contributes well to the open challenge A great sky that you''ve done well to bring out the lovely detail without blowing the highlights. The sliver of foreground serves well as an interesting base that has plenty to keep our interest until we inevitably look up to that fascinating sky whose textures and variety of colours are really quite captivating. A great exposure and composition well done and thanks for your entry Janine', '2016-08-08 07:42:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(7467722, 1185185, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that contributes well to the open challenge<br/> <br/>A lovely dusk seascape with the sun slowly sinking in the background. Your composition and exposure is good with a sufficiently but not too slow shutter speed to capture a fell of motion in the water without going to the extremes of slowness that are all the rage nowadays. Whilst it is pleasing I think it  would be nice to have a focus point of a ship or a bird or something to add another dynamic to the overall quality of the scene. Thanks for your entry Konrad</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that contributes well to the open challenge A lovely dusk seascape with the sun slowly sinking in the background. Your composition and exposure is good with a sufficiently but not too slow shutter speed to capture a fell of motion in the water without going to the extremes of slowness that are all the rage nowadays. Whilst it is pleasing I think it  would be nice to have a focus point of a ship or a bird or something to add another dynamic to the overall quality of the scene. Thanks for your entry Konrad', '2016-08-08 07:49:02.000000', NULL, 0),
